  "reason": "All five completed experiments are singleprofile; the multiprofile + aggregation axis is entirely unexplored and represents the largest remaining source of uncertainty. config_005 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scVI_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-conceptual-change from config_004 (RNA-only, singleprofile, scVI_n200): it tests whether aggregating multiple profiles (via average pooling) captures complementary per-profile signal that a single profile discards, while keeping the modality (RNA-only) and encoder (scVI) fixed to isolate the profile/aggregation effect from image or fusion confounds. If multiprofile + avgpool yields a meaningful gain over config_004's 0.520, it strongly motivates investing subsequent budget in multiprofile multimodal configurations (e.g., config_030/032); if it does not, we can deprioritize that entire branch and focus on encoder or image improvements. This is the highest-information-value experiment under the limited budget because it resolves a binary design question that gates many downstream configurations, and it does so with the minimal number of changed variables."
}

